{"id": "q0044", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3363812437, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 2, "query": "Conor lives near a beach and loves going there every day to have fun. On a particular week, he found 50 people at the beach on the first day. The next day, 20 more people were present at the beach than on the first day, and on the third day, the total number of people increased to twice the number that were there on the second day. If Conor saw an average of 60 people each day the rest of the week, calculate the total number of people Conor saw at the beach that week.\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0044.wav", "input_sha256": "385454744bd1bbe744521f7e5aca34d5e6802f4c5e630188c0b9a0e7db3b9214", "input_samples": 542800, "input_s": 33.925, "n_real_chunks": 34, "score": 0.3329, "act": 0.9985, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Day 1: 50 people Day 2: 50 + 20 = 70 people Day 3: 2 × 70 = 140 people Rest of the week = 4 days Average for those 4 days = 60 people per day People for the rest of the week: 4 × 60 = 240 Total people for the week: 50 + 70 + 140 + 240 = 500 Final numeric answer: 500", "expert_answer": "Day 1: 50 people  \nDay 2: 50 + 20 = 70 people  \nDay 3: 2 × 70 = 140 people  \n\nRest of the week = 4 days  \nAverage for those 4 days = 60 people per day  \n\nPeople for the rest of the week:  \n4 × 60 = 240  \n\nTotal people for the week:  \n50 + 70 + 140 + 240 = **500**\n\nFinal numeric answer: **500**", "transcript": "Connor lives near a beach and loves going there every day to have fun. On a particular week, he found 50 people at the beach on 