{"id": "q0098", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1952941619, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 2, "query": "Farmer Brown has 20 animals on his farm, all either chickens or cows. They have a total of 70 legs, all together. How many of the animals are chickens?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0098.wav", "input_sha256": "af06f4a12a31a8f2c9ce0a5c88ff339aac4423dce9c4cbe132c5c7fc730b61c2", "input_samples": 214000, "input_s": 13.375, "n_real_chunks": 14, "score": 0.1151, "act": 0.9974, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Let: \\(c\\) = number of chickens , \\(w\\) = number of cows Total animals: \\[ c + w = 20 \\] Chickens have 2 legs and cows have 4 legs. Total legs: \\[ 2c + 4w = 70 \\] From \\(c + w = 20\\), solve for \\(c\\): \\[ c = 20 - w \\] Substitute: \\[ 2(20 - w) + 4w = 70 \\] \\[ 40 - 2w + 4w = 70 \\] \\[ 40 + 2w = 70 \\] \\[ 2w = 30 \\] \\[ w = 15 \\] So there are 15 cows. Then: \\[ c = 20 - 15 = 5 \\] Final numeric answer: 5", "expert_answer": "Let:\n\n- \\(c\\) = number of chickens  \n- \\(w\\) = number of cows  \n\nTotal animals:\n\n\\[\nc + w = 20\n\\]\n\nChickens have 2 legs and cows have 4 legs. Total legs:\n\n\\[\n2c + 4w = 70\n\\]\n\nFrom \\(c + w = 20\\), solve for \\(c\\):\n\n\\[\nc = 20 - w\n\\]\n\nSubstitute:\n\n\\[\n2(20 - w) + 4w = 70\n\\]\n\n\\[\n40 - 2w + 4w = 70\n\\]\n\n\\[\n40 + 2w = 70\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2w = 30\n\\]\n\n\\[\nw = 15\n\\]\n\nSo there are 15 cows. Then:\n\n\\[\nc = 20 - 15 = 5\n\\]\n\nFinal numeric answer: **5**", "transcript": "Farmer Brown has 20 animals on his farm, all either chickens or cows. They have a total of 70 legs altogether. How many of the animals are chickens? Show your work and end with the final numeric answer.\n", "asr_s": 1.17, "expert_s": 3.63, "expert_input_samples": 214000, "expert_input_s": 13.375, "expert_input_sha256": "af06f4a12a31a8f2c9ce0a5c88ff339aac4423dce9c4cbe132c5c7fc730b61c2", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 3.961, "relay_synth_ms": 105874, "onset_chunk": 13, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0098_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "3f6d3c53a907b376b0b901fc1a9041b7eef23a68b7a088eba8471c0a31e029a5", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 192.28}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0098_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "99768908c556b59569787af74271e482cfbd4498a5d5a598bde0cbc716ab7c64", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0098_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "1fb8b769ed04647d1d91870862d569c96f5f61bd15dd6df1ad3a7391e807ce18", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.077, 1.138, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.075, 2.139, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.077, 3.134, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.077, 4.139, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.08, 5.142, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.08, 6.143, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.069, 7.124, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.08, 8.143, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.077, 9.14, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.084, 10.147, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.082, 11.149, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.078, 12.139, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.083, 13.147, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 13.375, 13.457, 14.136, 0, 24000, 0]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 13.375, "last_real_feed_done": 13.457, "onset": 14.136, "gate_read_done": 14.136, "fire": 14.136, "candidate_first_pcm": 14.136, "stall_note": 14.138, "stall_first_pcm": 14.977, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 14.977, "expert_req": 14.138, "expert_resp": 18.937, "relay_synth_start": 18.938, "relay_first_pcm": 19.865, "relay_synth_end": 124.814, "first_any_pcm": 14.136, "first_answer_pcm": 19.865, "session_end": 125.969}, "ttfa_answer_s": 6.49, "ttfa_any_s": 0.761}
{"id": "q0114", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3033147943, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 2, "query": "When converting $\\frac{31}{11111}$ to a decimal, the decimal turns out to be a repeating decimal. How many digits repeat in this repeating decimal?\n\nFor example, if you get the repeating decimal $0.\\overline{123},$ then your answer should be $3,$ and if you get $0.436\\overline{7},$ your answer should be $1.$\n\nSolve and give the final answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0114.wav", "input_sha256": "1aac0c2181a56089a0f15195816626de48285ef19be54fcca2f7a7a976ccc4e8", "input_samples": 384600, "input_s": 24.038, "n_real_chunks": 25, "score": 0.8941, "act": 0.9964, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "\\[ \\frac{31}{1110} \\] Factor the denominator: \\[ 1110=2\\cdot 3\\cdot 5\\cdot 37 \\] The factors \\(2\\) and \\(5\\) only affect the non-repeating part. The repeating cycle comes from: \\[ 3\\cdot 37=111 \\] We need the smallest \\(k\\) such that: \\[ 10^k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{111} \\] Check powers: \\[ 10^1=10 \\] \\[ 10^2=100 \\] \\[ 10^3=1000 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{111} \\] So the repeating block has length \\(3\\). \\[ \\boxed{3} \\]", "expert_answer": "\\[\n\\frac{31}{1110}\n\\]\n\nFactor the denominator:\n\n\\[\n1110=2\\cdot 3\\cdot 5\\cdot 37\n\\]\n\nThe factors \\(2\\) and \\(5\\) only affect the non-repeating part. The repeating cycle comes from:\n\n\\[\n3\\cdot 37=111\n\\]\n\nWe need the smallest \\(k\\) such that:\n\n\\[\n10^k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{111}\n\\]\n\nCheck powers:\n\n\\[\n10^1=10\n\\]\n\n\\[\n10^2=100\n\\]\n\n\\[\n10^3=1000 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{111}\n\\]\n\nSo the repeating block has length \\(3\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]", "transcript": "When converting frac 31 1110 dollars to a decimal, the decimal turns out to be a repeating decimal. How many digits repeat in this repeating decimal? For example, if you get the repeating decimal 0 overline 123, then your answer should be 3, and if you get 0.436 overline 7, your answer should be 1. ", "asr_s": 1.56, "expert_s": 7.3, "expert_input_samples": 384600, "expert_input_s": 24.038, "expert_input_sha256": "1aac0c2181a56089a0f15195816626de48285ef19be54fcca2f7a7a976ccc4e8", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 0.0, "relay_synth_ms": 75448, "onset_chunk": 24, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 60, "feed_lag_max_ms": 1133, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 6444, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0114_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "dd17d6cfa89b3def4494bf8216974378836d8f370a690df632aca5a3f746569d", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 138.48}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0114_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "0a37fcbf94260a88c5dd62692f395939736d730b4fc9146d28ccbe854f40bc47", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0114_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "51ba1a3081d67ae6d7ab3cf64bbb1a7e627a4df7e8bd11f4ee4570995935556d", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 61.0}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.08, 1.142, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.081, 2.144, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.075, 3.137, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.076, 4.137, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.08, 5.145, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.079, 6.142, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.081, 7.146, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.08, 8.145, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.08, 9.144, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.08, 10.141, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.086, 11.151, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.082, 12.145, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.084, 13.146, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.081, 14.142, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.086, 15.149, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.082, 16.145, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 17.0, 17.081, 17.143, 1, 0, 0], [17, 1, 18.0, 18.083, 18.144, 1, 0, 0], [18, 1, 19.0, 19.08